# libretranslate
msgid "**Trusted-Header SSO Bridge:**   When the oauth2-proxy SSO flavor is active, Snipe-IT's native `loginViaRemoteUser()` is enabled via the `Setting` model (`login_remote_user_enabled`, `login_remote_user_header_name = HTTP_X_FORWARDED_PREFERRED_USERNAME`). nginx gates `/login` through oauth2-proxy/Keycloak and injects the verified `X-Forwarded-Preferred-Username` header, which Snipe-IT matches against `users.username` (the user must pre-exist and be activated — sync them via LDAP) to mint a native `snipeit_session`. Visitors without a matching activated user silently fall through to the normal login form (no error). The password/LDAP login form stays available as a fallback (`login_common_disabled = 0`), and the in-app logout is redirected to the central OIDC end-session URL."
msgstr "**Trusted- Header SSO tiltas:** Kai autas2-proxy SSO skonio yra aktyvus, Snipe- IT gimtoji `loginViaRemoteUser()` per `Setting` modelis (`login_remote_user_enabled`, `login_remote_user_header_name = HTTP_X_FORWARDED_PREFERRED_USERNAME`). nginx vartai `/login` per autą2- proxy /Keycloak ir įkelia patikrintus `X-Forwarded-Preferred-Username` antraštė, kuri Snipe- IT atitinka prieš `users.username` (vartotojas turi iš anksto egzistuoti ir būti aktyvuotas - sinchronizuoti juos per LDAP) kalti gimtąją `snipeit_session`. Lankytojai be tinkamo aktyvuoto vartotojo tyliai patenka į įprastą prisijungimo formą (be klaidos). Slaptažodis / LDAP prisijungimo forma lieka prieinama kaip atsarginis (`login_common_disabled = 0`), ir in- app įrašas nukreipiamas į centrinį OIDC pabaigos sesijos URL."

# libretranslate
msgid "**Trusted-header SSO bridge:** Establishes the owner session from the oauth2-proxy identity (see below)."
msgstr "**Patikimiausias SSO tiltas:** Nustato savininko sesiją auto2- proxy identity (žr. toliau)."

