msgstr "Įkelia CA pasitikėjimą automatiškai ``TLS_MODE=self_signed`` (per ``CA_TRUST.*``), kad Playwright priima savarankiškai pasirašytas cert grandines"

# libretranslate
msgid "Inline `[RBAC.GROUP.NAME, ...] | path_join` MUST NOT be used: it scatters the path shape across dozens of files and makes future layout changes partial. Centralising the path in the plugin guarantees that a layout evolution stays a one-file change."
msgstr "Inline `[RBAC.GROUP.NAME, ...] | path_join` NEPRIVALO būti naudojamas: jis išsklaido kelio formą per dešimtys failų ir daro ateities maketas iš dalies. Centralizuojant įskiepio kelią užtikrinama, kad išdėstymo evoliucija išliks vieno failo kaita."

# libretranslate
msgid "Inline hashes are added ONLY if that directive does NOT include 'unsafe-inline'."
msgstr "Inline hash yra pridedamas TIK, jei ši direktyva neturi įtraukti 'unsafe-inline'."

# libretranslate
msgid "Inline shell in workflow files SHOULD stay limited to small command calls, environment wiring, or direct script invocation."
msgstr "Inline apvalkalas darbastalio failus SHOULD likti tik mažų komandų skambučius, aplinkos laidai, arba tiesioginis scenarijų introdukcija."

# libretranslate
msgid "Inlined keys observed today (non-exhaustive): `plugins`, `plugins_enabled`, `email`, `ldap`, `accounts`, `scopes`, `alerting`, `languages`, `company`, `default_quota`, `legacy_login_mask`, `site_name`, `token`, `modules`, `network`, `performance`, `preload_models`, `provision`, `features`."
msgstr "@ info: whatsthis (neišsami): `plugins`, `plugins_enabled`, `email`, `ldap`, `accounts`, `scopes`, `alerting`, `languages`, `company`, `default_quota`, `legacy_login_mask`, `site_name`, `token`, `modules`, `network`, `performance`, `preload_models`, `provision`, `features`."

# libretranslate
#, python-brace-format
msgid "Input (env): ``APP_ID``. Optional ``INFINITO_APP_VARIANTS`` (JSON ``{app_id: variant_index}``, set per round by the matrix orchestrator) selects the active variant so a variant that pins ``services.*`` flags to ``false`` prunes those providers from the closure instead of the provision step pulling them in from the variant-free base config. In-process callers that already hold the round map pass it as ``derive_includes(app_id, variants=...)``; the env var is read only when that argument is omitted."
msgstr "Įvestis (env): ``APP_ID``. Neprivaloma ``INFINITO_APP_VARIANTS`` (JSON ``{app_id: variant_index}``, nustatyti per turas matricos orkestro) parenka aktyvų variantą taip, kad kaiščiai variantas ``services.*`` @ info: whatsthis ``false`` nutrina tuos paslaugų teikėjus nuo uždarymo, o ne nuo tiekimo etapo, traukdamas juos iš nestandartinės bazės konfigūracijos. In- procesinių skambinančiųjų, kurie jau laiko apvalų žemėlapį perduoti jį kaip ``derive_includes(app_id, variants=...)``; env var skaityti tik tada, kai šis argumentas praleidžiamas."

# libretranslate
msgid "Input name -> the literal its marker segment renders when set."
msgstr "Įvesties pavadinimas - > pažodinis jo žymeklio segmentas rodo, kai nustatyta."

# libretranslate
msgid "Input name -> the literal its value segment opens with, template order."
msgstr "Įvesties pavadinimas - > pažodinis jo vertės segmentas atsidaro su, šablonas tvarka."

# libretranslate
msgid "Inputs"
msgstr "Įvediniai"

# libretranslate
msgid "Inputs (env): ``APP_ID``, ``INFINITO_DOMAIN`` (the SPOT for the deployment domain; defined in ``default.env`` and exported by ``scripts/meta/env/load.sh``; the development inventory reads the same env var for the play's ``DOMAIN_PRIMARY``), ``HOSTS_ENTRY_IP`` (optional; address the domains map to, default ``127.0.0.1``)."
msgstr "Įvediniai (env): ``APP_ID``, ``INFINITO_DOMAIN`` (diegimo srities SPOT; apibrėžta ``default.env`` ir eksportuoja ``scripts/meta/env/load.sh``; plėtros inventorius skaito tą patį env var žaisti ``DOMAIN_PRIMARY``), ``HOSTS_ENTRY_IP`` (neprivaloma; adresas domenų žemėlapyje, numatytasis ``127.0.0.1``)."

# libretranslate
msgid "Inputs (env): ``APP_ID``, ``INV_PATH`` (default ``/tmp/inv/devices.yml``). Optional ``INFINITO_APP_VARIANTS`` (consumed by ``derive_includes``)."
msgstr "Įvediniai (env): ``APP_ID``, ``INV_PATH`` (numatytasis ``/tmp/inv/devices.yml``). Neprivaloma ``INFINITO_APP_VARIANTS`` (suvartoti ``derive_includes``)."

# libretranslate
msgid "Inputs (env): ``INV_DIR`` — inventory dir holding ``host_vars/*.yml`` (default ``/tmp/inv``)."
msgstr "Įvediniai (env): ``INV_DIR`` - inventorization dir holding ``host_vars/*.yml`` (numatytasis ``/tmp/inv``)."

msgid "Inputs (env): ``NFS_IP``, ``MGR_IP``, ``MGR``, ``OUT_PATH`` (default ``/tmp/swarm-nfs-extras.yml``), ``KEY_PATH`` (default ``/tmp/swarm-nfs-admin.key``). A second ed25519 keypair is generated at ``INFINITO_SWARM_BACKUP_KEY`` (SPOT: default.env) and its public half lands in ``users.backup.authorized_keys`` so the DR drill's backup host can pull over the ``user-backup`` ssh-wrapper. The ``applications`` block written into the extras file carries the ``local-2-device`` mount/target/source device paths, which is all the DR drill reads back from it. The deploy-facing overrides, including ``remote-2-local.backup_providers`` (derived per round from ``utils.tests.swarm.backup_repos``), are baked by the matrix orchestrator into the provisioner's host_vars merge (INFINITO_VARS_PAYLOAD), NOT into the extras file: extra-vars replace the whole inventory ``applications`` dict and would strip every generated credential. ``users`` carries the same hazard for the same reason, and its authorized_keys travel the same merge channel. The deploy-facing twin ``<OUT_PATH stem>.deploy.yml`` therefore carries everything except ``applications`` and ``users``."
msgstr ""

# libretranslate
msgid "Inputs come from the merged application config (``services.<key>.image`` and ``services.<key>.version``). ``image=`` and ``version=`` keyword overrides bypass those values for ad-hoc references (e.g. side-car init containers that do not appear in the services map)."
msgstr "Įėjimai iš sujungtos programos konfigūracijos (``services.<key>.image`` ir ``services.<key>.version``). ``image=`` ir ``version=`` raktažodis peržengia šias reikšmes ad- hoc nuorodoms (pvz., savivarčiai automobiliai konteineriai, kurie nepateikiami paslaugų žemėlapyje)."

# libretranslate
msgid "Inputs the retrigger reads from the job log rather than the run title."
msgstr "Įveda regaiduktas skaito iš darbo žurnalo, o ne paleisti pavadinimą."

# libretranslate
msgid "Inputs 🔧"
msgstr "Įvediniai 🔧"

# libretranslate
msgid "Inside a play the process boundary is the task: Ansible forks a fresh worker per task, so `_MERGED_APPLICATIONS_CACHE` starts empty in every worker. `get_merged_applications` therefore also accepts the play-scoped carrier fact `_INFINITO_APPLICATIONS_RENDERED` (payload plus cache key, parked once by the constructor stage) and serves it when the key matches. See [applications.md](../../docs/contributing/artefact/files/plugins/lookup/applications.md) for the contract."
msgstr "Viduje žaisti proceso riba yra užduotis: Patartina šakės šviežios darbuotojas vienai užduočiai, todėl `_MERGED_APPLICATIONS_CACHE` prasideda tuščias kiekvieno darbuotojo. `get_merged_applications` todėl taip pat priima play- scoped vežėjas faktas `_INFINITO_APPLICATIONS_RENDERED` (naudingoji apkrova plius talpyklos klavišą, stovėjo vieną kartą statybininkas etape) ir tarnauja, kai raktas atitinka. Žr. [applications.md](../../docs/contributing/artefact/files/plugins/lookup/applications.md) sutarties atveju."

